\section{Methodology}

\subsection{Document Processing}

This dossier was prepared using the following methodology:

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Document Intake:} Original documents were scanned at 300 DPI resolution.
\item \textbf{Optical Character Recognition:} Text was extracted using Google Cloud Vision API.
\item \textbf{Entity Extraction:} People, properties, organizations, and locations were identified using AI-assisted extraction (Claude API).
\item \textbf{Relationship Mapping:} Connections between entities were inferred from document context.
\item \textbf{Verification:} All AI-extracted data is marked as TIER\_3\_AI pending human verification.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Verification Tiers}

\begin{description}
\item[TIER\_3\_AI] Automatically extracted by artificial intelligence. Not yet verified by a human analyst. May contain errors or misinterpretations.

\item[TIER\_2\_ANALYST] Verified by a trained analyst. The analyst has reviewed the source document and confirmed the extracted information is accurate.

\item[TIER\_2\_INSTITUTIONAL] Verified against institutional records (e.g., property registries, vital records offices).

\item[TIER\_1\_CERTIFIED] Certified by a licensed professional (attorney, notary). Suitable for legal proceedings.
\end{description}

\subsection{Limitations}

\begin{itemize}
\item OCR accuracy varies with document quality. Handwritten documents may have lower accuracy.
\item AI extraction may miss entities or relationships not explicitly stated in the text.
\item Historical documents may use outdated terminology or conventions.
\item Translation from Spanish was performed automatically and may contain errors.
\item This dossier presents \textbf{forensic facts}, not legal conclusions.
\end{itemize}

